1
00:00:00,406 --> 00:00:06,525
(Q11（单选）) It's great to see so many members of the Twinning Association here tonight.

2
00:00:06,525 --> 00:00:20,655
Since the twinning link between our two towns, Stanthorpe here in England and Malatte in France, was established, the relationship between the towns has gone from strength to strength.

3
00:00:20,655 --> 00:00:28,504
Last month, 25 members of the association from Stanthorpe spent a weekend in Malatte.

4
00:00:28,504 --> 00:00:32,332
Our hosts had arranged a great programme.

5
00:00:32,332 --> 00:00:38,923
[Q11干扰项（C） ； 仅提及， 不符合especially] We learned how cheese is produced in the region and had the chance to taste the products.

6
00:00:38,923 --> 00:00:50,067
[Q11答案句（B） highlight = especially， + Q11干扰项A： 排除依据： 否定表达 - cancel] The theme park trip had to be cancelled, but we all had a great time on the final boat trip down the river – that was the real highlight.

7
00:00:50,067 --> 00:00:57,548
(Q12) This is a special year for the Association because it's 25 years since we were founded.

8
00:00:57,548 --> 00:01:04,337
[Q12干扰项（C）： Malatte小镇计划， 和题干中的Stanthorpe不符] In Malatte, they're planning to mark this by building a footbridge in the municipal park.

9
00:01:04,337 --> 00:01:12,831
[Q12答案句（A） poplar tree = tree 上下义] We've been discussing what to do here and we've decided to plant a poplar tree in the museum gardens.

10
00:01:12,831 --> 00:01:19,804
[Q12干扰项（B） 排除依据： 否定表达： weren't happy about] We considered buying a garden seat to put there, but the authorities weren't happy with that idea.

11
00:01:19,804 --> 00:01:26,408
(Q13) In terms of fundraising to support our activities, we've done very well.

12
00:01:26,408 --> 00:01:39,164
[Q13答案句（B） record = most， Q13干扰项（C） 仅提及] Our pancake evening was well attended and made record profits. And everyone enjoyed the demonstration of French cookery, which was nearly as successful.

13
00:01:39,164 --> 00:01:48,138
[Q13干扰项（A）仅提及] Numbers for our film show were limited because of the venue so we're looking for somewhere bigger next year.

14
00:01:48,138 --> 00:01:59,147
(Q14) We're looking forward to welcoming our French visitors here next week, and I know that many of you here will be hosting individuals or families.

15
00:01:59,147 --> 00:02:05,102
The coach from France will arrive at 5 pm on Friday.

16
00:02:05,102 --> 00:02:15,118
[Q14答案句（C） have dinner in house = meal at home ， Q14干扰项（B） 排除依据， 否定， rather than.     eat out = restaurant] Don't try to do too much that first evening as they'll be tired, so have dinner in the house or garden rather than eating out.

17
00:02:15,118 --> 00:02:21,329
The weather looks as if it'll be OK so you might like to plan a barbecue.

18
00:02:21,329 --> 00:02:29,663
[Q14干扰项A， 不符合 first evening] Then the next morning's market day in town, and that's always a good place to stroll round.

19
00:02:29,663 --> 00:02:41,840
(Q15) [Q15答案句（A） + Q15干扰项B- 偷换概念 football] On Saturday evening, we'll all meet up at the football club, where once again we'll have Toby Sharp and his band performing English and Scottish country songs.

20
00:02:41,840 --> 00:02:53,540
[Q15干扰项（C） 去年的一个quiz，不符合时间限定] Toby will already be well known to many of you as last year he organised our special quiz night and presented the prizes.&nbsp;

21
00:02:53,540 --> 00:03:04,662
(Q16（地图）) Now on Sunday, we'll be taking our visitors to Farley House. You may not all be familiar with it, so here's a map to help you.

22
00:03:04,662 --> 00:03:19,455
You can see the car park at the bottom of the map. There's an excellent farm shop in the grounds where our visitors can buy local produce – it's in the old stables, which is the first building you come to.

23
00:03:19,455 --> 00:03:25,997
They're built round a courtyard, and the shop's in the far corner on the left.

24
00:03:25,997 --> 00:03:30,798
There's also a small café on the right as you go in.

25
00:03:30,798 --> 00:03:36,592
(Q17) I know that one or two of our visitors may not be all that mobile.

26
00:03:36,592 --> 00:03:44,092
The main entrance to the house has a lot of steps so you might want to use the disabled entry.

27
00:03:44,092 --> 00:03:48,451
This is on the far side of the house from the car park.

28
00:03:48,451 --> 00:03:53,921
(Q18) Children will probably be most interested in the adventure playground.

29
00:03:53,921 --> 00:04:01,013
That's at the northern end of the larger lake, in a bend on the path that leads to the lake.

30
00:04:01,013 --> 00:04:04,518
There's lots for children to do there.&nbsp;

31
00:04:04,518 --> 00:04:13,911
(Q19) There are a number of lovely gardens near the house. The kitchen gardens are rectangular and surrounded by a wall.

32
00:04:13,911 --> 00:04:18,620
They're to the north-east of the house, quite near the smaller lake.

33
00:04:18,620 --> 00:04:24,310
They're still in use and have a great collection of fruit and vegetables.

34
00:04:24,310 --> 00:04:30,661
(Q20) The Temple of the Four Winds is a bit more of a walk – but it's worth it.

35
00:04:30,661 --> 00:04:37,887
Take the path from the car park and go past the western sides of the stables and the house.

36
00:04:37,887 --> 00:04:48,713
Then when the path forks, take the right-hand path. Go up there with the woods on your left and the temple is right at the end.

37
00:04:48,713 --> 00:04:51,213
There are great views over the whole area.

